<title>USA: Sparks 1997 soy acres at 64.5 mln, corn 81.5-trade.</title>
<headline>Sparks 1997 soy acres at 64.5 mln, corn 81.5-trade.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Memphis-based analytical firm Sparks Companies on Friday pegged 1997 U.S. soybean acreage at 64.5 million acres and corn at 81.5 million acres, trade sources said.</p>
<p>That compared with USDA's 1996 figures of 64.2 million acres of soybeans and 79.5 million acres of corn.</p>
<p>Traders said Sparks' soybean estimate was slightly below expectation while the corn figure was slightly above expectation.</p>
<p>Sources at Sparks declined to comment on the numbers.</p>
<p>((--Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
